 ## Overview
-MTL-FeatureNet is a feature extraction network designed for multi-task learning that improves the accuracy and relevance of features extracted from a single 2D input view [S1]. It addresses the challenge of adapting a unified feature representation to diverse task requirements by integrating task dynamic attention modulation and a dynamic adapter layer [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF encodings which map coordinates to radiance properties directly, MTL-FeatureNet operates on 2D image features to support multiple downstream tasks simultaneously, distinguishing it from sibling architectures like [SUDS](14964-suds.md) or [Rip-NeRF](15532-rip-nerf.md) which focus on 3D coordinate encoding for volume rendering.
+MTL-FeatureNet is a feature extraction network for multi-task learning that handles demands of multiple tasks by improving the accuracy and relevance of features extracted from a single 2D toy view [S1]. It addresses the challenge of adapting a unified feature representation to diverse task requirements by integrating task dynamic attention modulation and a dynamic adapter layer [S1].
 
