 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Task Correlation:** The weight $v_{ij}$ in the cross-task loss depends on the correlation between tasks. If tasks are highly correlated, $v_{ij}$ should reflect this to prevent redundant feature learning; if uncorrelated, it should allow divergence [S1]. The method for dynamically adjusting $v_{ij}$ is not specified in the sources [G].
-*   **Attention Modulation:** The term $\exp(TR_i)$ scales the attention logits. If $TR_i$ is large, this can lead to numerical instability or overly sharp attention distributions. Proper scaling or normalization of $TR_i$ may be required [G].
+*   **Task Correlation:** The weight $v_{ij}$ in the cross-task loss depends on the correlation between tasks [S1]. The method for dynamically adjusting $v_{ij}$ is not specified in the sources [G].
